# A site package page object that derives the Fluid template name from the
# backend layout of the page, the way bk2k/bootstrap-package does.
#
# The block below "templateName" is a faithful copy of that package's
# "page.10.templateName" - reproduced here rather than depended on, because what
# the test pins is the mechanism, not one third party release of it.
# "case = uppercamelcase" is GeneralUtility::underscoredToUpperCamelCase(),
# which lowercases the whole string before it camel cases it on underscores, and
# "split" runs before "case" in the stdWrap order. So "pagets__AcademicProgram" arrives at
# Fluid as "Academicprogram" unless the extension sets the name itself.
#
# This file is included *before* the TypoScript of the extension, which is the
# order a site package and an extension static template have in an installation:
# the theme defines the page object, the extension refines it.
page = PAGE
page {
  10 = FLUIDTEMPLATE
  10 {
    templateRootPaths.10 = EXT:academic_programs/Tests/Functional/Pages/Fixtures/Templates/
    templateName = TEXT
    templateName {
      cObject = TEXT
      cObject {
        data = pagelayout
        required = 1
        case = uppercamelcase
        split {
          token = pagets__
          cObjNum = 1
          1.current = 1
        }
      }
      ifEmpty = Default
    }
  }
}
